A little over two hours the council consumed before it finished.

We walked the long corridor toward the next place of work. Behind Chachamaru, only I remained. The other staff officers had received their instructions and departed. Apparently work had no shortage of places waiting for it.

Kaam khatam? No. The meeting was finished. Work had merely changed its address. This distinction was becoming clear to me. Kill a meeting, and from its body come instructions; each instruction grows into more work, and eventually somebody calls another meeting to ask why none of it is finished. A creature that reproduced by being completed. If only the professor had studied this instead of tsurugi. No underground reservoir required. Four chairs and somebody to say &#x27;the next matter.&#x27;
